WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.430
Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:08.680
The current administration is likely to behave
outrageously all the way to the end of the

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.980
end, which is going to be Wednesday, January
20th.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.990
And in the meantime, we're expecting a lot
of action in different ways.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:21.029
Yesterday, House Democrats did introduce articles
of impeachment against Donald Trump.

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:23.859
This is the second impeachment against Donald
Trump.

00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:28.710
And Trump could be very quickly heading to
being the only president to be impeached two

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.710
times.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.440
This article of impeachment filed yesterday
is for inciting the mob that attacked the

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.910
capital last week.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:43.860
And we now have a question mark as to what
will the next 24 to 36 hours look like.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.440
And I'll talk about that with you in a moment.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:54.610
Nancy Pelosi and the rest of her caucus of
the constituency of Democrats in the House

00:00:54.610 --> 00:01:00.320
are also simultaneously working the 25th Amendment
angle, which again, I don't believe is actually

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.360
going to go anywhere but there.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:07.170
They want Vice President Mike Pence, along
with Donald Trump's cabinet, to intervene

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.969
and simply remove Donald Trump.

00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:14.200
Now, as I've said before, removal of Trump
via the 25th Amendment was warranted years

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:20.130
ago, and it continues to be impeachment of
Donald Trump again, is warranted.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:25.959
And it is the right thing to do, even though
neither is likely to remove Trump even a minute

00:01:25.959 --> 00:01:30.169
short of when his term will end at noon Eastern
Time next Wednesday.

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:36.139
But these are responsibilities that our lawmakers
have, not political calculations to be made.

00:01:36.139 --> 00:01:39.770
And so I have said that they should indeed
go forward.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:44.799
And the schedule, as we now understand it,
and because things are moving so quickly,

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:47.189
by the time you listen to this, there may
have been some modification.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:56.700
The House is likely to vote tonight, formally
calling on Vice President Pence to strip Trump

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.729
of the presidency via the 25th Amendment.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:05.130
So the process so far has been articles of
impeachment introduced yesterday.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.959
We hear from Nancy Pelosi that the articles
of impeachment will be voted on potentially

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:15.910
tomorrow at 9:00 a.m. if Pence does not act
to remove Donald Trump via the 25th, which,

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:19.189
of course, requires the cabinet as well.

00:02:19.189 --> 00:02:26.060
And if indeed that doesn't happen, then and
only then would there be an impeachment vote.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:31.859
And so this is The New York Times is describing
this as a standoff between two branches of

00:02:31.859 --> 00:02:32.859
government.

00:02:32.859 --> 00:02:36.609
House Democrats are pressuring Mike Pence
to intervene.

00:02:36.609 --> 00:02:42.230
And so that that's between the House and and
the executive.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:47.290
And then at the same time, you are potentially
going to see a standoff between Democrats

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:52.400
and Republicans, not so much within the House,
where the Democrats appear to very clearly

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.280
have the votes to impeach Trump a second time.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.650
But with regard to what's going to happen
in the Senate, and it has already been discussed

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:04.469
that there is, of course, not time to conduct
a Senate impeachment trial between now or

00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:08.170
what is more likely going to be tomorrow,
the impeachment vote and the end of Donald

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.170
Trump's presidency.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:12.560
That would be just one week, but that is not
a problem.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.670
Legally speaking, a president can be impeached
after they leave office.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.810
They can be convicted on impeachment after
they leave office.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.920
But if you start that in two weeks or in three
weeks, what do you do to the first 100 days

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.530
of Joe Biden?

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:30.099
When we are desperately needing to accelerate
vaccine distribution, we are in the middle

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:33.530
of a disastrous handling of a global hundred
year pandemic.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.249
And Joe Biden presumably plans to do quite
a bit in his first 100 days.

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:42.330
So the idea has already been floated of you
vote to impeach during Trump's term and then

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:47.000
you hold those articles of impeachment, delaying
the Senate trial for a period of several months.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.189
We don't we just don't know at this point
what's going to happen now.

00:03:50.189 --> 00:03:57.209
At the same time, you might recall that Donald
Trump and Mike Pence hadn't met since the

00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:02.400
riotous insurrection on Wednesday and reportedly
hadn't even spoken.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.109
We've now learned, thanks to New York Times
reporting, that Trump met with Pence yesterday

00:04:07.109 --> 00:04:13.340
for the first time since he publicly denounced
Mike Pence on Twitter as the riotous insurrection

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:14.340
was happening.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.329
Trump taking to Twitter and saying Pence didn't
he didn't do it.

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:19.570
He just didn't do the right thing.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:23.889
And the meeting was reportedly more than an
hour long.

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:29.560
And it it you know, there are varying reports
from what happened, but it's being described

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:36.380
as a fraught peace summit where the conversation
is described as good.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:41.780
But it's unclear whether Pence said, listen,
the pressure for me to use the 25th is growing

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:46.190
and you should do this, that or the other
thing to prevent me from having to do it.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:51.750
Although every indication we've received so
far is that it is very unlikely that Mike

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.880
Pence is going to act in that way.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:58.470
So for me, the real issue here is.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:05.110
Not one of political calculation, and it is
not one of legacy for people like Pence or

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.130
other Republicans.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:12.540
I've already said all of these Republicans
that in the last 14 days, 16 days of Trump's

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:17.270
presidency have come out and said this is
impeachable or he should resign or he should

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.879
be removed or this is now over the line.

00:05:19.879 --> 00:05:24.819
These are not people who deserve really any
praise from us for what they are doing.

00:05:24.819 --> 00:05:31.129
It doesn't take courage when Trump is at his
weakest and when much of the Republican Party,

00:05:31.129 --> 00:05:34.640
but certainly much of the country has turned
against him and he's leaving anyway.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.690
It doesn't take courage at that point to come
out and say, yeah, he should go.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:44.060
It would have taken courage maybe to do it
before when they actually would have been

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.139
at electoral risk.

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:48.400
I'm talking about Republican senators and
members of Congress and others.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.620
And at this point in time, it's merely a calculation
about self-preservation.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.639
There are Republicans who have calculated
and maybe they are right that at this point

00:05:56.639 --> 00:06:02.500
distancing from Trump 14 days before he's
gone rather than a day after he's gone is

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.500
better for them.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.729
And that's really what this is about.

00:06:05.729 --> 00:06:09.550
Even people like Lindsey Graham, we talked
about Lindsey Graham on January 6th, or I

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:13.280
guess it was really January 7th, very early
January 7th in the morning.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:19.080
He he gave this speech saying we Biden's the
president and we must and we we can't hold

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.080
this.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.620
And some people said, wow, that was a great
speech by Lindsey Graham.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.990
Lindsey Graham is one of the slipperiest brown
nosers of Trump.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:31.620
And within hours of that, as we covered yesterday,
Lindsey Graham was on Fox News begging for

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.690
mercy for Trump and saying, listen, Trump
did the right thing.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.919
He lowered the temperature and he made a,
you know, a useful, productive statement saying

00:06:38.919 --> 00:06:42.729
Joe Biden, well, he actually didn't say Joe
Biden, there will be a transition and I'm

00:06:42.729 --> 00:06:44.289
committed to it.

00:06:44.289 --> 00:06:50.910
Even the people that seem to be sort of talking
sense are really trying to play both sides.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.189
And there are there are a few exceptions.

00:06:52.189 --> 00:06:58.170
I mean, listen, Mitt Romney, at least he stopped
playing both sides years ago.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:01.439
He met with Trump early during the transition.

00:07:01.439 --> 00:07:04.360
It looked at the 2016 transition.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:08.819
Mind you, it looked like maybe Romney was
being considered for secretary of state and

00:07:08.819 --> 00:07:12.830
you went and had Frogs' legs or turtle soup
or whatever with Trump.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.580
And then he wasn't considered.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.870
And earlier, Romney said what was on his mind.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:23.240
I disagree with Romney in that I think his
condemnation should have been much stronger.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:29.169
I disagree with Romney in that Romney is still
a religious Republican and I'm not.

00:07:29.169 --> 00:07:33.940
But at least my belief is Romney was telling
us what he really felt for years, whereas

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:37.639
with Lindsey, it's flip flopping constantly
and playing both sides.

00:07:37.639 --> 00:08:18.419
So impeachment vote tomorrow at 9:00 a.m.,
the most likely scenario, and we'll let you

00:08:18.419 --> 00:08:55.830
know what happens.

